    normally.

 -- CyberVitexus <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:40:22 +0200

mcprack (0.2.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stamp alembic to head immediately after the db.create_all()
    bootstrap fallback, not just skip it once alembic_version exists.
    Previously a bootstrapped database (create_all() ran because
    alembic_version was missing, e.g. because an earlier postinst bug
    prevented 'flask db upgrade' from ever running) was left with no
    alembic_version row at all, so the next 'flask db upgrade' tried to
    run the very first migration from scratch and failed with 'table
    already exists'.

 -- CyberVitexus <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Tue, 28 Jul 2026 03:29:27 +0200

mcprack (0.2.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix 0.2.13's env-permission fix not applying on upgrade: chmod/chown
    of /etc/mcprack/env only ran inside the 'file doesn't exist yet'
    branch, so upgrades from pre-0.2.13 packages kept the broken 0600
    perms and still failed db upgrade / create-admin. Now applied
    unconditionally on every postinst configure.
  * Fix AppStream metadata: rename mcprack.metainfo.xml to
    cz.vitexsoftware.mcprack.metainfo.xml to match the component's
    <id>, per spec. Fix the <icon type="stock"> reference ("mcp-logo")
    which named an icon nothing installed anywhere; now ships and
    installs static/mcprack-app-icon.svg to
    /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/ under a matching stock
    name. Also repoint the broken screenshot URL at the file that
    actually exists in the repo.

